% composition-series: CBC Modern Canadian Bridges — pilot
% composition-grade: 4
% composition-elements: syncopation across the middle of the bar; sixteenth-note pairs; major/minor contrast through E/E-flat and A/A-flat; crescendo, decrescendo and fermata; two-part ostinato; sixteen-bar ABBA form
% composition-listen: Claudia Bouvette — "Amour écran" (2026), a Francophone dream/electro-pop single and CBC Music Top 20 selection dated 9 November 2026
% composition-listen-url: https://www.bonsound.com/fr/release/amour-ecran/
% composition-bridge: Hear how airy synthesizer timbres, an insistent electronic pulse and an 1980s-coloured major/minor haze can support intimate French-language pop writing.
% composition-context: Claudia Bouvette is a Montréal singer-songwriter. "Amour écran" was written with Soran Dussaigne and released by Bonsound; the label describes it as modern dream pop with atmospheric synthesizers.
% composition-distance: Original French classroom text, melody, C/Cm contrast and ostinato; no words, melodic cell, synth patch, bass line or chord progression from "Amour écran" is used.
% improv: {"id":"A","bars":"5-8","role":"synth or barred-instrument player","prompt":"Choose the B-section colour","choices":["bright major third","shadowed minor third","alternate each bar"],"replyBars":4}
% improv: {"id":"B","bars":"13-16","role":"whole class","prompt":"Choose the final texture","choices":["melody alone","add two-note ostinato","fade to whispered rhythm"],"replyBars":4}
% dossier-function: original Grade 4 Francophone electro/dream-pop listening bridge; students sing a syncopated ABBA song, compare parallel major and minor colour, and select the final texture in real time
% dossier-elements: sixteen bars in 4/4; C-major A sections and parallel C-minor B section using E-flat and A-flat; C4-C5 melody range; eighths, quarters, a dotted-quarter/eighth syncopation, paired sixteenths, whole note and final fermata; crescendo/decrescendo; optional C-G two-note ostinato; ABBA form
% dossier-practice: Rehearsal key C/C minor; written range C4-C5. Quarter note = 100 target, start at 76. Speak the French rhythm with a fluent model, clap the middle-of-bar syncopation, sing the major A, lower E and A for B, then add the ostinato. Do not perform the text publicly before language review.
% dossier-accompaniment: Newly authored generic electronic-pop loop C-Am-F-G for A and Cm-Ab-Fm-G for B. Classroom version uses bass roots, soft shaker eighths and a neutral sustained keyboard; do not imitate Bouvette's synth sounds or production.
% dossier-lyrics: Original French text: "Lumière d'écran, je vois la nuit; je choisis l'ombre ou bien la couleur. Une voix répond, puis je réponds; nos deux chemins reviennent au coeur." Intended sense: screen light, I see the night; I choose shadow or colour; one voice answers, then I answer; our two paths return to the heart. A Francophone reviewer must correct idiom and sung stress.
% dossier-honesty: AI-assisted original course composition, 11 November 2026; not a Claudia Bouvette work, translation, arrangement or soundalike. The genre label identifies a listening comparison only.
% dossier-licence: CC0 1.0 for melody, text, chords, ostinato and ABC; "Amour écran" and its recording remain copyrighted.
% dossier-respect: Centre a current Francophone Canadian artist and use French as living creative language, not decoration. Pronunciation, idiom and cultural context require Francophone review before publication.
% dossier-review: Grade 4 teacher, Francophone language reviewer, Francophone Canadian music educator, second score reader and student trial; all reviews still required
